<!-- NowPlayingWidget — the "Currently Watching" card on the HOME SCREEN (spec §7), for the
     hours when nothing is playing: the last episode the viewer watched, and one tap back
     into it. iOS home + lock-screen widget (Core/Widgets, the ImageWidget target) and the
     Android Glance widget render THIS file; the Live Activity twin is NowPlayingActivity.dsx,
     whose lockscreen slot is this same card so the two surfaces cannot drift.

     THIS IS A SNAPSHOT DOCUMENT, not a screen (StackWidgets.md, live-surfaces-dsx.md): a
     widget process runs no JSE and fetches nothing, so the dialect is the small one — stacks,
     text, image, spacer, `{{ dsx.variable.<key> }}` holes only (no ternaries, no calls), and
     every colour is a LITERAL. The literals are checked mirrors of Components/parts/Theme.dsx
     (widgetCard #0E0E10 · ink3 #8E8E93 · sheetCard #1C1C1E · accentWidget #FF3D5D · ink
     #FFFFFF · stage #000000), the same rule every <style> block already lives under.

     THE VARIABLES the app publishes (Components/parts/NowPlayingSurface.dsx, through
     dsx.module.widget.layout({ layout: 'NowPlayingWidget', vars, images })):
       show    the show id            idx   the 1-based episode index
       title   the show title         ep    the "EP.n" label, pre-formatted
       caption "Currently Watching"   cta   "▶︎ Continue Watching" — both LOCALIZED BY THE
               APP (`localize()`), because a snapshot process has no string table: the
               words arrive as vars, and the 13 locales this app ships reach the card
       poster  the poster's FILE PATH on this device — the module fetched the https PNG twin
               into the shared container (live-surfaces/images.json); a widget paints only
               what is already on the device
       mark    the app mark's file path, the same way
     A hole the app left empty renders empty; the card renders regardless.

     THE TAP is the ROOT's href (live-surfaces/links.json): a relative path joins the app's
     own URL scheme — `/watch/<show>/<idx>` becomes `shortdrama://watch/<show>/<idx>` — and
     the Router's inbound door lands it on the player, cold or warm. The whole card is the
     link because a small widget honours nothing else.

     ONE DOCUMENT, A LAYOUT PER FAMILY (StackWidgetDocument): the <widget> root's first visual
     child is the card every family renders; a <small>/<medium>/<large>/<rectangular>/
     <circular>/<inline> slot would override it for that family. The medium card is the card
     here (the reference's own size), so no slot is declared; the <head> is declaration-only
     and never rendered. Android's Glance has no families and renders the same child.

     "▶︎" IS A TEXT GLYPH, DELIBERATELY (U+25B6 with the text-presentation selector U+FE0E — without it iOS draws the blue emoji tile, measured on the lock screen): the snapshot dialect has no unified-icon element (the
     in-app renderer draws the shared catalog; a widget process has no catalog and an SF
     symbol has no Android twin), so the one glyph the spec writes into the label is the one
     character that renders identically on both lanes. Filed in PLAN.md §6 as the ask.

     SIZING is by content, not by frame: the layout box carries padding/background/radius/
     grow, and the column's height comes from its rows — poster 108 + 16pt padding = the
     140pt a medium widget holds. The title keeps the spec's two lines. -->
<widget>
  <head>
    <expects variable="show"/>     <!-- the show id -->
    <expects variable="idx"/>      <!-- the 1-based episode index -->
    <expects variable="title"/>    <!-- the show title -->
    <expects variable="ep"/>       <!-- "EP.n", pre-formatted -->
    <expects variable="caption"/>  <!-- "Currently Watching", localized by the app -->
    <expects variable="cta"/>      <!-- "▶︎ Continue Watching", localized by the app -->
    <expects variable="poster"/>   <!-- the poster's file path on this device (module-fetched) -->
    <expects variable="mark"/>     <!-- the app mark's file path, the same way -->
  </head>
  <hstack bg="#0E0E10" radius="16" paddingh="14" paddingv="10" spacing="12" align="top" grow="width"
            href="/watch/{{ dsx.variable.show }}/{{ dsx.variable.idx }}">
    <image src="{{ dsx.variable.poster }}" width="72" height="108" radius="8" fit="cover"/>
    <vstack align="leading" spacing="0" grow="width">
      <hstack align="top" spacing="8">
        <vstack align="leading" spacing="2" grow="width">
          <text size="12" color="#8E8E93" lines="1">{{ dsx.variable.caption }}</text>
          <text size="20" weight="bold" color="#FFFFFF" lines="2">{{ dsx.variable.title }}</text>
          <text size="12" color="#8E8E93" lines="1">{{ dsx.variable.ep }}</text>
        </vstack>
        <hstack bg="#1C1C1E" radius="6" padding="3">
          <image src="{{ dsx.variable.mark }}" width="14" height="14" fit="contain"/>
        </hstack>
      </hstack>
      <spacer/>
      <hstack bg="#FF3D5D" radius="10" paddingv="7" paddingh="12" grow="width" align="center">
        <text size="14" weight="bold" color="#FFFFFF" lines="1">{{ dsx.variable.cta }}</text>
      </hstack>
    </vstack>
  </hstack>
</widget>
